**Proposition 8.1 (the precise kernel obstruction).** Restrict to initial
prepared bracket states with common public initialization. For the task consisting
of all public original numerical/TM57 observations, the task kernel is universal
on $\{U_x\}$, whereas the initial-tree or literal response task has equality
kernel on $x$. An expression computed solely from those numerical histories and
authentic archive copies cannot be sufficient for the latter task. If the task
instead includes an unprojected original successor whose source field is the
actual tree, its kernel also separates every $U_x$.

Proof. Theorem 4.2 makes every original public experiment constant. The initial
queries $p_iL$ separate any two unequal bit vectors, giving the literal task
kernel exactly equality. Any map of constant numerical data is constant, so
cannot determine these responses. For the full-successor task, a legal Read
preserves the actual source in its successor. Thus two different $U_x$ give
different full successor values even when their Read labels and every public
micro-observation agree. Replacing that hidden field by its numerical projection
would define a different task.

